0.2.16
Config:
    Trader trades can be specified by weight

Great Spell:
    Increment Moon Phase (pretty expensive, maintains relative position of moon/sun)

Spells:
    Kill Still Fish (makes stackable) (free)
    Attach/Detach Hook

Patterns:
    Envirnomental:
        Get DayTime (Distinct from GameTime which Hexal adds, as DayTime takes sleeping in bed into account)
        Get Biome (From blockPos)
        Get Weather (TODO)
        Get Medium (from bobber)
        Get Dimension (0 args)
        Get Moon Phase (0 args)
        Get Structures (From blockPos)
        Get Climate (from blockPos) (This is the chunk climate thing Tide uses for temperature)

    Fish:
        Patterns to check for all the conditinos a fish may have (Most of the ones I could think of at least)

Items:
    Added a chair variant
    Added 1 Rare Fish
    Added 1 Legendary Fish
    Added Chain fishing Line
    Added Sampling Focus Bobber (cosmetic) (1.21.1 prevents me from making the item model look how I want...)
    Added Rocky Rod
        reduces luck and increases speed
    Unlucky bait renamed to odious bait
    Added unlucky bait
        reduces luck
    Crystal Shrimp Fried Rice (costs two crystal shrimp) (how did they do it?)
        applies clarity I and luck I for 13 and 6.5 minutes respectively
    Removed unneeded recipes


Balance Changes:
    Modified some of trader's fishing trades
    Modified trader spawn chance
    Trade now spawns at most once every 2 hours per player (I forget if this was 0.2.15 or if I did it just after)

Mechanics:
    Music Disc was made less miserable to get

Notable Bugfixes:
    I'm putting this here so I don't forget to bring it up: fixed client-side tide rendering/minigame bugs with kilt+sable (the minigame should work)
    Made the fish I had added work better (I hope). (No longer axolotl-based)

If I added or changed anything else I forgot because it was a bugfix or insignificant, I think I fixed some bad spell circle oversights at least, when I looked over it again...
Tried to fix the create mod hat position for my creature, too.